  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 405.15 Water Supply Quality Sampling",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 405.15 Water Supply Quality Sampling.\n\n(a) Water quality sampling for new, hydrofractured, or deepened community wells shall comply with Env-Dw 302 or Env-Dw 305, as applicable.\n\n(b) The collection date of the samples taken in accordance with (a) above, shall be no greater than 6 months prior to the time the final design application is submitted to the department.\n\n(c) Samples taken in accordance with (a) above, shall be taken after at least 3 well volumes have been pumped from the well.\n\n(d) The owner shall have the laboratory results submitted to the department as originals or copies of the originals. Re-typing or re-writing the data shall not be acceptable.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for Env-Dw 405) #10612, eff 6-1-14; ss #14158, eff 12-25-24 (formerly Env-Dw 405.16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html"
